# pytest conventions

- Name tests after the observable behavior and keep each test focused on one outcome.
- Use fixtures for repeated setup and `tmp_path` for filesystem isolation.
- Assert meaningful outputs, side effects, and errors rather than implementation details.
- Run the smallest relevant test selection while iterating, then run the complete suite before handoff.
- Mock IO aggressively to keep unit tests fast, deterministic, and to prevent side-effects in live systems.